# Two ORA-01403 summaries (OER, TTC message type 0x04) Oracle 23ai Free sent
# the client bundled in gvenzl/oracle-free:23-slim during one session, captured
# on dbbat's upstream leg. TNS Data payloads: two data-flag bytes, then the TTC
# message, ending in the 0x1d end-of-response marker.
#
# They are the 64-bit OCI summary object -- the same fields as the 32-bit one
# the Instant Client 23.3 gets, at wider offsets (oerFixed64Layout):
#
#   call status  u32 @1    = 1
#   ECID seq     u16 @5    = this OER's sequence
#   error number u16 @12   = 1403
#   cursor id    u16 @18   = 2
#   call number  u32 @49   = the sequence of the client call it answers (7, 12)
#   RetCode      u32 @132  = 1403 again -- the invariant the learner validates
#   row count    u64 @136, two 4-byte tail fields, then the message CLR at 152
#
# Handed the 32-bit frame instead, this client never finishes the call. One
# frame per non-comment line.


